WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.057
Reflective practice is structured learning from experience.

2
00:00:04.057 --> 00:00:13.089
It is the deliberate habit of looking at real work, asking what happened, examining the evidence, and deciding what should change next time.

3
00:00:13.089 --> 00:00:19.060
Experience gives raw material, but reflection turns that material into reusable learning.

4
00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:27.327
Without reflection, a person can repeat the same activity many times while carrying forward the same assumptions and mistakes.

5
00:00:27.327 --> 00:00:32.226
Reflection is different from memory, reaction, analysis, and rumination.

6
00:00:32.226 --> 00:00:33.833
Memory recalls an event.

7
00:00:33.833 --> 00:00:36.359
Reaction expresses how the event felt.

8
00:00:36.359 --> 00:00:38.809
Analysis breaks the event into parts.

9
00:00:38.809 --> 00:00:41.947
Reflection connects the event to future action.

10
00:00:41.947 --> 00:00:49.755
It asks what the experience reveals about decisions, assumptions, context, tradeoffs, skills, systems, and behavior.

11
00:00:49.755 --> 00:00:54.271
The purpose is not to relive the past; it is to improve the next attempt.

12
00:00:54.271 --> 00:01:02.844
Reflective practice matters in technical work, learning, leadership, communication, incident response, and skill development.

13
00:01:02.844 --> 00:01:05.906
A developer can reflect on a debugging session.

14
00:01:05.906 --> 00:01:08.279
A team can reflect after an incident.

15
00:01:08.279 --> 00:01:11.723
A leader can reflect after a difficult conversation.

16
00:01:11.723 --> 00:01:14.173
A learner can reflect after practice.

17
00:01:14.173 --> 00:01:20.832
In each case, the point is to notice patterns that would otherwise remain hidden inside the pace of work.

18
00:01:20.832 --> 00:01:24.889
This course treats reflection as practical and non-clinical.

19
00:01:24.889 --> 00:01:30.247
It is not vague journaling, performative note-taking, blame, or self-criticism.

20
00:01:30.247 --> 00:01:33.232
It is also not a reason to delay action forever.

21
00:01:33.232 --> 00:01:43.566
The goal is to turn real work into reusable learning: better questions, better judgment, better habits, better systems, and more reliable future performance.
